From: BrokenShine <xchai404@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] zig-mode: degrade single-token alternation for cl-ppcre 2.1.1

Guix's sbcl-cl-ppcre 2.1.1 rejects single-branch (:alternation "x")
patterns with PPCRE-SYNTAX-ERROR ("Encountered alternation without
choices"), while newer Quicklisp releases accept them.  Lem's zig-mode
passes a one-element token list ("_") through its tokens helper.
Degrade to the bare string, which matches identically.

Upstream-status: not submitted upstream; works around a Guix-only
cl-ppcre version gap.  Can be dropped once Guix ships cl-ppcre >= 2.1.2
(if it accepts single-branch alternations).

diff --git a/extensions/zig-mode/zig-mode.lisp b/extensions/zig-mode/zig-mode.lisp
index d8ad8346..52f65193 100644
--- a/extensions/zig-mode/zig-mode.lisp
+++ b/extensions/zig-mode/zig-mode.lisp
@@ -12,7 +12,11 @@
 (defun tokens (boundary strings)
   "Create a regex pattern for matching a list of tokens."
   (let ((alternation
-          `(:alternation ,@(sort (copy-list strings) #'> :key #'length))))
+          ;; cl-ppcre 2.1.1 rejects single-branch (:alternation "x");
+          ;; degrade to the bare string, which matches identically.
+          (if (cdr strings)
+              `(:alternation ,@(sort (copy-list strings) #'> :key #'length))
+              (car strings))))
     (if boundary
         `(:sequence ,boundary ,alternation ,boundary)
         alternation)))
